join Marloch (Marloch_normal) center
Marloch (Marloch_satisfied): You came back.
catherine: So did you.
Marloch (Marloch_what): I live here.
catherine: Do you?
Marloch (Marloch_angry): What sort of question is that?  It’s the least of pleasantries, yes, I’m not from here. You came all this way for nothing.
catherine: Thank you for reminding me…
Marloch (Marloch_satisfied): The universe can be unfair from time to time.
Marloch (Marloch_angry): You seem disappointed. Is it because I refused to help you?
catherine: Because I thought the stories were true. Perhaps that is what hurts most.
catherine: My mother spent years telling me about this place.
Marloch (Marloch_what): And what did she say?
catherine: That you were kind and powerful and understanding and.. whatever. Not like this.
Marloch (Marloch_satisfied): Your mother was wrong.
catherine: I don’t think she was, at least some of it is true. I believe you weren’t like someone bad before. Not as bad as you might look. I also don’t think you enjoyed becoming what you are.
Marloch (Marloch_angry): You know nothing about me.
catherine: No. But I know what it is like to be trapped inside something you never chose.
Narrator: Catherine's eyes begin to water.
catherine: I'm afraid. I am afraid of dying.
catherine: I still want to live. I want to travel. I want to see things. I want to be old and complain about my knees.
Marloch (Marloch_normal): The universe can be unfair from time to time.
- Go against fate.
	catherine: I don't care what your universe or fate or whatever you are saying. I want what I want.
	Marloch (Marloch_angry): As if you have any possibility of getting it on your own.
	Marloch (Marloch_angry): You just sound desperate and angry. Your anger will change nothing.
	catherine: And you? Is that true that you helped people before?
	Marloch (Marloch_angry): Yes it's true. But it's all in the past now.
	catherine: So what is the difference between my anger and your anger. You will also change nothing.
	catherine: Stuck in this dying town full of.. nothing.
	leave Marloch
	set {EndingTracking.marloch_feeling} -= 1.0
- Accept your fate.
	catherine: You know what? Life has given me lemons without any juice. I just wanna give up.
	Marloch (Marloch_what): I didn't expect you to take it like that.
	catherine: I am almost used to it. Almost.
	Marloch (Marloch_what): You don't have what I want. And you are not willing to push for more. I guess you don't really want to live.
	catherine: I still do, but not to the detriment of others.
	Marloch (Marloch_satisfied): You are quite special, quite interesting.
	Marloch (Marloch_satisfied): I am sure this won't be the last time we meet.
	leave Marloch
	set {EndingTracking.marloch_feeling} += 1.0
